{"title": "Chair's letter", "blocks": [
("h1", "Chair's letter"),
("p", "Dear shareholder, 2025 was the year in which Kerrowan stopped being a promising mid-sized instrument maker and started to look like the leader in its niche. Our people delivered record revenue, a meaningfully higher margin and a full product launch, all while the business absorbed a change of Chief Financial Officer and the opening of a new site in the Netherlands."),
("p", "I want to begin by thanking Graham Leckie, who retired as Chief Financial Officer in January 2025 after eleven years with the company. Graham steered Kerrowan through its move to the main market and through the difficult supply years of 2021 and 2022. He was succeeded by Priya Raman, who joined us in February 2025 from a listed engineering group and has already sharpened the way we allocate capital."),
("p", "The Board met eleven times during the year, including two full-day sessions on strategy. Most of that strategic work went into Course 2028, the plan described on page 6, which the Board approved in October 2025. We spent time in particular on the balance between growing the software business and protecting the cash generation of our established buoy and sonar products."),
("p", "Shareholders will have seen that the Board is recommending a final dividend that brings the total for the year to 11.4 pence per share, compared with 9.8 pence for 2024. This reflects our confidence in the cash flow of the business while keeping enough headroom for acquisitions such as the one completed after the year end."),
("p", "Governance remained a priority. During the year we carried out an external review of Board effectiveness, led by an independent adviser, which concluded that the Board works well but should spend more time on technology risk. In response, the Audit and Risk Committee now receives a cyber security report at every meeting rather than twice a year."),
("p", "Finally, I would like to thank our customers, many of whom have relied on Kerrowan instruments in difficult waters for more than two decades, and every one of our colleagues. Their work is what turns a plan into results."),
("p", "Margaret Oduya, Chair, 19 March 2026"),
]},
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- page 3
{"title": "Chief Executive's review", "blocks": [
("h1", "Chief Executive's review"),
("p", "When I became Chief Executive in April 2021, I said that Kerrowan's next chapter would be about turning excellent instruments into complete monitoring systems. In 2025 that idea became visible in our numbers. Group revenue rose to £184.6m, and for the first time more than one in seven pounds of revenue came from customers who buy hardware and Harbourline software together."),
("p", "Three things stood out for me. The first was the launch of the Tidewatch T5 in September 2025, our first buoy designed from the start to stream data directly into Harbourline. Early demand was strong, and we shipped 310 units in the last four months of the year. The second was the opening of our Rotterdam service centre in June 2025, which put engineers within a day's travel of most of our European customers and cut average repair turnaround for European customers from 19 days to 8 days."),
("p", "The third was less visible but just as important: the steady improvement in our operating margin. Better pricing on the storm-rated Tidewatch T3-S, a richer mix of software and lower freight costs together lifted the Group operating margin by one and a half percentage points. That improvement came without cutting research spending, which grew faster than revenue."),
("p", "Not everything went to plan. A firmware fault in the first batch of Kestrel 400X sonar units shipped in March forced us to recall 37 units for an on-site update, and the episode cost us roughly £0.6m and some goodwill with two survey customers. We have since added an extra stage of field testing before any new firmware is released, and the fault has not recurred."),
("p", "Looking ahead, our priority is to execute Course 2028 with discipline. The acquisition of Brightwater Acoustics in February 2026, described on page 22, adds acoustic modems to our range and a strong engineering team in Canada. I am grateful to everyone at Kerrowan for a year of real progress."),
("p", "Daniel Achterberg, Chief Executive"),
]},
