# ---------------------------------------------------------------- page 5
{"title": "Our company and history", "blocks": [
("h1", "Our company and history"),
("p", "Kerrowan Marine Systems was founded in 1994 by the oceanographer Isla Kerrowan and the electronics engineer Tomas Ferreira, who met while working on a university wave-measurement project. Their first workshop was a rented boat shed on the harbour at Port Lennox, a few hundred metres from today's headquarters."),
("p", "The company's first commercial product, the Tidewatch T1 buoy, went on sale in 1997. It measured wave height, water temperature and current speed and reported by radio to a shore station. Port authorities in Scotland and Norway were the first customers, and that focus on ports has shaped the company ever since."),
("p", "Growth in the late 1990s led to the opening of the Port Lennox factory in 1998. The company then spent several years building a reputation for buoys that survive the North Atlantic. In 2006 Kerrowan listed its shares on the main market of the London Stock Exchange, raising funds to expand internationally."),
("p", "In 2012 Kerrowan bought Sondera Acoustics, a small sonar specialist based in Bergen, Norway. Sondera's side-scan sonar technology became the foundation of the Kestrel product line, which now accounts for roughly a third of Group revenue."),
("p", "Software followed hardware. Harbourline, a cloud platform that brings together data from buoys, sonar and vessel traffic systems, was launched in 2018. It was first offered free to existing buoy customers and moved to a paid subscription model in 2020."),
("p", "In 2019 the company acquired a second factory, at Port Lenham in Cornwall, England, from a defence electronics supplier that was leaving the area. Port Lenham now assembles most of the Kestrel sonar range, while Port Lennox makes buoys. The similar names of the two sites are a coincidence that our logistics team has learned to live with."),
("p", "Today Kerrowan sells to customers in 41 countries. Isla Kerrowan retired from the Board in 2016 but remains the company's honorary president, and still visits the Port Lennox workshop most weeks."),
]},
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- page 6
{"title": "Strategy: Course 2028", "blocks": [
("h1", "Strategy: Course 2028"),
("p", "Course 2028 is the Group's strategy for the four years from 2025 to 2028. It was developed by the executive team over the summer of 2025 and approved by the Board in October 2025. It replaces the earlier plan, Horizon 2025, whose revenue target of £175m was exceeded a year early."),
("p", "The strategy has a simple premise: customers increasingly want answers rather than instruments. A harbour master wants to know whether a channel is safe for a deep-draught vessel, not to read raw sonar files. Kerrowan is therefore building complete monitoring systems in which its hardware feeds Harbourline, and Harbourline turns the data into decisions."),
("h2", "The four pillars"),
("p", "Pillar one, Connected hardware, means that every new Kerrowan instrument will connect natively to Harbourline from 2026. Pillar two, Software growth, aims to double Harbourline annual recurring revenue between 2025 and 2028. Pillar three, Service close to the customer, extends the model of the Rotterdam service centre to North America and Asia. Pillar four, Responsible operations, commits the Group to net zero emissions from its own operations by 2032."),
("h2", "Targets for 2028"),
("table", [["Target", "2028 goal", "2025 actual"],
           ["Group revenue", "£260m", "£184.6m"],
           ["Operating margin", "17%", "14.7%"],
           ["Harbourline annual recurring revenue", "£45m", "£22.8m"],
           ["Share of revenue from connected systems", "40%", "15%"],
           ["Renewable electricity in own operations", "100%", "71%"]]),
("p", "The Board expects most of the growth to be organic, but Course 2028 allows for bolt-on acquisitions that add technology or customers. The Group has set itself a limit of net debt of no more than one times operating profit for any acquisition."),
("p", "Progress against each target will be reported every year. The Remuneration Committee has linked part of the long-term incentive plan for executives to the revenue and margin targets, as described on page 21."),
]},
